	You are completely correct:  harder is not always fine.  Let
me think aloud:


	I've read the "General Fixes and Modified Features" for each
release since about 3.4.0.  I believe that Nethack has gotten a bit
easier, overall.  [1]

	This YANI makes the game harder:

   o  Unspoiled players will be killed at least once before they
      catch on.  (This is a feature.  Nethack will have more things
      in it you have to figure out:  the game will be "larger".)

   o  Experienced players will sometimes misjudge exactly when
      they're tough enough to take out a hit team.  (Feature.)

   o  Experienced players will sometimes slaughter hit teams very
      early in the game.  This makes the game easier, especially when
      they get dragon scales out of it.  This counterbalances the
      previous item.

   o  Players will sometimes be killed by the game, instead of by
      their own ignorance or error.  (Rock mole or dwarf steals the
      gold, and a third level character is facing a dragon.)  (I
      view this as a drawback to the YANI, even if it only affects
      0.2% (?) of all games by expert players.)


	This YANI would affect Nethack's difficulty by more than 
almost any recent change.  For all that, it doesn't change the
difficulty much.  Unlike some other YANIs I've had, I don't feel
the need to add a second change to rebalance the game.

	I don't like the "player killed by the game" bit.  If I
were coding this up, I would grope around for a fix.  Say, add
in the Grudge Patch and give vault guards grudges against rock
moles, xorns, and dwarves.  Then make the hit team peaceful if 
you're a non-dwarf and the theft wasn't your fault.



[1]	The most striking change towards "easier" I recall are non-
rotting lichen corpses, which pets don't eat and which greatly help
early problems with starvation.  The most striking change towards
"harder" I recall is moving two quest bosses out of LOS of the 
stairs to protect 'em from being insta-slept.  (Taking athames away
from starting wizards was roughly balanced by the +oFB.)


